From cb4e0448a3c8fb7a4de467c53f69d68aef24209f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ikloog <ikloog@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:54:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Locate the file: the playing track's file in your file
 manager
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A trigger run by hand -- from Workspace › Run, so from the command palette
too -- is now told what plays, as a panel is: `playing`, with the engine
playing it, or null with nothing playing. Started any other way it is told
nothing of it. ADR-0295 has an amendment.

With it comes an official plugin, Locate the file, off until enabled: the
playing track's file, from Workspace › Run, or the tracks chosen, from the
context menu -- the first of each folder -- shown in the system's file
manager (Finder on macOS, the file selected; elsewhere FileManager1, else
xdg-open on the folder), Tandem, or a shell command of one's own, {} the
file and {folder} its folder. An engine's music folder can be mapped to
where it is mounted here; a file not here is said to be so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
